{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"2cd007193e678edf","name":"card_unit_seaforth_highlanders","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/Breakthrough/units/card_unit_seaforth_highlanders","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"SEAFORTH HIGHLANDERS","text":"Has +3 attack on the enemy turn.","flavorText":"The Seaforth Highlanders is an infantry regiment of the British Army, mainly associated with the northern Highlands of Scotland. The regiment existed from 1881 to 1961 and fought in WWI and WWII, plus other minor conflicts. During WWII the Seaforth Highlanders were split into 7 battalions which served separately in various theaters of the war. The 1st was deployed in Malaya in 1940 and served in the Burma Campaign. The 2nd and 4th Battalions were captured in the Battle of France in 1940. The 2nd was reformed and fought in the Second Battle of Alamein, the Tunisian Campaign and the Italian Campaign. Later the battalion participated in Operation Overlord and the Allied invasion of Germany. The 5th and 6th Battalions served in the Italian campaign and was then deployed in North-West Europe. The 7th Battalion fought in Operation Epsom in France in 1944 and then served in North-West Europe.","faction":"Britain","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":4,"operationCost":1,"attack":1,"defense":7},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_seaforth_highlanders","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_seaforth_highlanders_title","SourceString":"SEAFORTH HIGHLANDERS","LocalizedString":"SEAFORTH HIGHLANDERS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":1,"defense":7,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_seaforth_highlanders_text","SourceString":"Has +3 attack on the enemy turn.","LocalizedString":"Has +3 attack on the enemy turn."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_seaforth_highlanders_history","SourceString":"The Seaforth Highlanders is an infantry regiment of the British Army, mainly associated with the northern Highlands of Scotland. The regiment existed from 1881 to 1961 and fought in WWI and WWII, plus other minor conflicts. During WWII the Seaforth Highlanders were split into 7 battalions which served separately in various theaters of the war. The 1st was deployed in Malaya in 1940 and served in the Burma Campaign. The 2nd and 4th Battalions were captured in the Battle of France in 1940. The 2nd was reformed and fought in the Second Battle of Alamein, the Tunisian Campaign and the Italian Campaign. Later the battalion participated in Operation Overlord and the Allied invasion of Germany. The 5th and 6th Battalions served in the Italian campaign and was then deployed in North-West Europe. The 7th Battalion fought in Operation Epsom in France in 1944 and then served in North-West Europe.","LocalizedString":"The Seaforth Highlanders is an infantry regiment of the British Army, mainly associated with the northern Highlands of Scotland. The regiment existed from 1881 to 1961 and fought in WWI and WWII, plus other minor conflicts. During WWII the Seaforth Highlanders were split into 7 battalions which served separately in various theaters of the war. The 1st was deployed in Malaya in 1940 and served in the Burma Campaign. The 2nd and 4th Battalions were captured in the Battle of France in 1940. The 2nd was reformed and fought in the Second Battle of Alamein, the Tunisian Campaign and the Italian Campaign. Later the battalion participated in Operation Overlord and the Allied invasion of Germany. The 5th and 6th Battalions served in the Italian campaign and was then deployed in North-West Europe. The 7th Battalion fought in Operation Epsom in France in 1944 and then served in North-West Europe."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Breakthrough","returnSet":"ECardSetEnum::Homefront","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnStartofTur